        <body>These flowports are not bound to the ARM target because only a product definition property type can be assigned to it.</body>
      </ownedComment>
      <ownedComment xmi:id="_18_4_1_271a0567_1526463115295_131770_212501" xmi:uuid="8466df40-f7ed-4d6e-a670-bb800f263a5a" xmi:type="uml:Comment">
        <annotatedElement href="../../../../SysML_ARM/SYSML_ARM_AP242.xmi#_2_attr_SYSML_ARM-Part_version-of_product"/>
        <body>Part.Versions provides the mapping of Part_version.of_product</body>
      </ownedComment>
      <ownedComment xmi:id="_18_0_5_45e01bd_1455715823026_950924_42909" xmi:uuid="e6f9078c-e738-4680-814d-0621e34cdd79" xmi:type="uml:Comment">
        <annotatedElement xmi:idref="_18_4_1_e120334_1499417193168_61072_23712"/>
        <body>A PartVersion is an identification of a version of a part. It serves as the collector of the data characterizing a realizable object in various application contexts. &lt;note&gt; A PartVersion is a part that may be produced, consumed, used to produce other PartVersion objects, or offered to the market. &lt;/note&gt;&lt;note&gt; The collection of defining information may be incomplete, i.e., not all of the PartView objects needed to define a PartVersion are associated with the PartVersion. &lt;/note&gt;&lt;note&gt; The set of all PartVersion objects of a Part represents the history of the Part within a specific life-cycle stage or over its complete life cycle. &lt;/note&gt;&lt;note&gt; A PartVersion does not have to be referenced by any PartView. &lt;/note&gt;&lt;note&gt; The following additional data can be assigned to a PartVersion: ActivityMethod, Approval, Certification, Contract, DateTimeString, Document, DocumentVersion, DocumentDefinition, File, Effectivity, InformationUsageRight, BreakdownElement, IndividualPartView, Occurrence, PartVersion, RequirementView, Project, PropertyValue, ExternalPropertyDefinition, PropertyDefinition, RequirementView, SecurityClassification, and WorkRequest.&lt;/note&gt;</body>
      </ownedComment>
      <name>PartVersion</name>
