    <packagedElement xmi:id="_18_4_1_e120334_1499417193154_583949_23682" xmi:uuid="c9e096ae-bfb6-4353-9bf9-aba9f2b5d1bb" xmi:type="uml:Class">
      <ownedComment xmi:id="_18_4_1_271a0567_1551195476744_893617_120621" xmi:uuid="00928942-a65f-429e-bdec-825db414fb34" xmi:type="uml:Comment">
        <annotatedElement href="../CommonResources/CommonResources.xmi#_18_4_1_290014c_1550847743191_208266_98071"/>
        <body>These flowports are not bound to the ARM target because only a product definition property type can be assigned to it.</body>
      </ownedComment>
      <ownedComment xmi:id="_18_0_5_45e01bd_1455714717706_938331_42873" xmi:uuid="2c726628-5d4c-43ea-b649-9ec1bdc18a89" xmi:type="uml:Comment">
        <annotatedElement xmi:idref="_18_4_1_e120334_1499417193154_583949_23682"/>
        <body>An Occurrence is an occurrence of an object in a product structure that is defined either by a PartView, another Occurrence, or as a ProductConfiguration. &lt;example&gt;In the case of a car, the Item 'wheel' is defined once. Its PartVersion carries all the information necessary to define the wheel (such as its shape) independent of its usage. Additionally, there are 5 Occurrence objects for this wheel since there are 5 equal wheels used in a car: Front-left, front-right, rear-left, rear-right, and spare wheel. Each of these instances may carry additional information such as placement or function. Each Occurrence is a DefinitionBasedOccurrence, or a SpecifiedOccurrence. &lt;/example&gt;</body>
      </ownedComment>
      <name>Occurrence</name>
      <generalization xmi:id="_18_4_1_290014c_1533819369991_485718_105683" xmi:uuid="0ed87b6a-48c7-4dd9-8c8b-393d253cc43d" xmi:type="uml:Generalization">
