      <ownedComment xmi:id="_18_0_5_45e01bd_1455715383049_571687_42887" xmi:uuid="5034fb44-0799-4a39-8597-b112853d816f" xmi:type="uml:Comment">
        <annotatedElement xmi:idref="_18_4_1_e120334_1499417193163_499955_23702"/>
        <body>A Part is an identification of definition of a part. It collects the definitional information of the versions of a part. A Part shall always be categorized as 'piece part', 'product', 'software', 'tool', or 'raw material' using a ClassSelect. &lt;note&gt; A Part does not represent an actual physical object of the real world. &lt;/note&gt;&lt;note&gt; A Part may be either a single piece part, an assembly of arbitrary complexity, a raw material, or a tool. &lt;/note&gt;&lt;example&gt; In the context of cars, a Part may be the car as a whole, the assembly of the engine, the car body, a fender, the side window glass, grease, or a stamping die. &lt;/example&gt;&lt;example&gt; In the context of aeroplanes, a Part may be the air plane as a whole, the assembly of the engine, the body of the air plane, a fender, the side window glass, grease, or a stamping die. &lt;/example&gt;&lt;note&gt; A Part is identified by an organization. The definition of the domain of uniqueness and the mechanism for guaranteeing the uniqueness of Part id are outside the scope of this capability. &lt;/note&gt;</body>
      </ownedComment>
      <name>Part</name>
