    </packagedElement>
    <packagedElement xmi:id="_19_0_4_b1702d9_1702993887082_62150_60050" xmi:uuid="e68b8616-bd8d-4e80-aae4-8dd8e2fdbaf8" xmi:type="uml:Class">
      <ownedComment xmi:id="_19_0_4_b1702d9_1702993887601_239826_60153" xmi:uuid="b87fb165-e478-4f0a-a8a9-3b51bde2fe05" xmi:type="uml:Comment">
        <annotatedElement xmi:idref="_19_0_4_b1702d9_1702993887082_62150_60050"/>
        <body>An AlternatePartVersionRelationship is a type of PartVersionRelationship where the relating part version represents the base part version and the related part version represents the alternate part version. The relationship established by the AlternatePartVersionRelationship is not symmetric: if part version B is an alternate part version for part version A, part version A is not implied to be an alternate part version for part version B. &lt;note&gt;If a part version is an alternate for another part version, it is understood that there is no interest in keeping track of which part version, the base or any alternates specified, is used as a specific instance of the base part version within a part structure.&lt;/note&gt;&lt;note&gt;An organization may track design changes for a base part version, and establish effectivity conditions for the use of that base part version in various assemblies to be manufactured.&lt;/note&gt;&lt;note&gt;An AlternatePartVersionRelationship for which the base part version is an assembly involves that the entire part structure of the alternate part version may be used in place of the base part version and its part structure.&lt;/note&gt;&lt;note&gt;This concept usually refers to form, fit, function, and quality. Additional properties such as performance, noise, endurance, or reliability may also be considered as a prerequisite for the replacement.&lt;/note&gt;&lt;example&gt;Two bolt versions of the same size exist. One bolt version has a square head and the other has a hexagonal head. The two bolt versions are considered equivalent with respect to form, fit, and function: they both have sufficiently close physical shape, they take up the same space when used, and they both serve to fasten two things together. Thus, one of these two bolt versions could be considered to be an alternate part version for the other bolt version.&lt;/example&gt;</body>
      </ownedComment>
      <name>AlternatePartVersionRelationship</name>
      <ownedRule xmi:id="_19_0_4_b1702d9_1702993887083_863682_60051" xmi:uuid="973e40f1-0954-4a49-8813-d45867c0b9c8" xmi:type="uml:Constraint">
        <ownedComment xmi:id="_19_0_4_b1702d9_1702993887605_526783_60189" xmi:uuid="379c1cfb-8597-4329-99fd-da12621c136e" xmi:type="uml:Comment">
          <ownedComment xmi:id="_19_0_4_b1702d9_1702993887631_537982_60376" xmi:uuid="74b1a18a-2a62-4058-a8d9-ea2568f1bda0" xmi:type="uml:Comment">
            <body>UR1: SELF\PartVersionRelationship.Relating, SELF\PartVersionRelationship.Related;</body>
          </ownedComment>
          <body>EXPRESS</body>
        </ownedComment>
        <ownedComment xmi:id="_18_4_1_65b021e_1721295758553_474305_151280" xmi:uuid="4b10fd99-2c4d-46e6-a096-21f0eb66e6d8" xmi:type="uml:Comment">
          <ownedComment xmi:id="_18_4_1_65b021e_1721295758553_808308_151281" xmi:uuid="996ff59c-9e43-4db9-9fad-df69e0b375a9" xmi:type="uml:Comment">
            <body> &lt;sch:rule context="//*[@uid and substring-after(@xsi:type,':')='AlternatePartVersionRelationship']"&gt; &lt;sch:let name="entity_name" value="if(@xsi:type) then substring-after(@xsi:type,':') else name()"/&gt; &lt;sch:let name="uid" value="@uid"/&gt; &lt;sch:let name="relatingUid" value="../@uid"/&gt; &lt;sch:let name="relatedUid" value="Related/@uidRef"/&gt; &lt;sch:assert test="not(//*[@uid and substring-after(@xsi:type,':')='AlternatePartVersionRelationship' and ../@uid = $relatingUid and Related/@uidRef = $relatedUid and @uid != $uid])"&gt; The combination of the related part version and the relating part version shall be unique. { -entity_name:&lt;sch:value-of select="$entity_name"/&gt; -entity_uid:&lt;sch:value-of select="$uid"/&gt; -rule_name:UR1 -attribute_name:RelatingAndRelatedUids -attribute_value:&lt;sch:value-of select="concat($relatingUid, ',', $relatedUid)"/&gt; } &lt;/sch:assert&gt; &lt;/sch:rule&gt;</body>
          </ownedComment>
          <body>Schematron</body>
        </ownedComment>
        <ownedComment xmi:id="_19_0_4_b1702d9_1702993887605_530618_60188" xmi:uuid="b8c9c41e-20f0-4302-8ac2-8aead95921a8" xmi:type="uml:Comment">
          <annotatedElement xmi:idref="_19_0_4_b1702d9_1702993887083_863682_60051"/>
          <body>the combination of the related part version and the relating part version shall be unique. </body>
        </ownedComment>
        <name>UR1</name>
        <constrainedElement xmi:idref="_19_0_4_b1702d9_1702993887082_62150_60050"/>
        <specification xmi:id="_19_0_4_b1702d9_1702993887605_24441_60187" xmi:uuid="e0f6b16f-0d3f-4924-9291-078e1083eb7b" xmi:type="uml:OpaqueExpression">
          <body>AlternatePartVersionRelationship::allInstances() -&gt;isUnique(Sequence{Relating, Related})</body>
          <language>OCL2.0</language>
        </specification>
      </ownedRule>
      <generalization xmi:id="_19_0_4_b1702d9_1702993887604_656210_60180" xmi:uuid="17bf4b23-2859-4fde-9d20-b7cf5a771d73" xmi:type="uml:Generalization">
        <general xmi:idref="_18_4_1_e120334_1499417193170_235850_23714"/>
      </generalization>
      <ownedAttribute xmi:id="_19_0_4_b1702d9_1702993887602_87594_60154" xmi:uuid="eb5016ce-26cf-4bfb-b31b-11bc8f2ad634" xmi:type="uml:Property">
        <ownedComment xmi:id="_19_0_4_b1702d9_1702993887626_760795_60307" xmi:uuid="b4732485-9fa5-4e0c-8d44-3a3403a75cac" xmi:type="uml:Comment">
          <annotatedElement xmi:idref="_19_0_4_b1702d9_1702993887602_87594_60154"/>
          <body>the word or set of words describing the requirements that are covered by both the base part version and the alternate part version and therefore are the basis for the statement regarding the capability of replacing the base part version by the alternate part version. &lt;note&gt; Additional properties such as performance, noise, endurance, or reliability may also be considered as a prerequisite for the replacement in addition to form, fit, function, and quality.&lt;/note&gt; The value of this attribute need not be specified. </body>
        </ownedComment>
        <name>Criteria</name>
        <visibility>public</visibility>
        <type href="../CommonResources/CommonResources.xmi#_18_4_1_e120334_1499417193151_806926_23674"/>
        <lowerValue xmi:id="_19_0_4_b1702d9_1702993887626_645898_60308" xmi:uuid="9382bc22-0406-437f-ad55-15a61056b0a0" xmi:type="uml:LiteralInteger"/>
        <aggregation>composite</aggregation>
        <association xmi:idref="_19_0_4_b1702d9_1702993898318_72324_62395"/>
      </ownedAttribute>
      <ownedAttribute xmi:id="_19_0_4_b1702d9_1702993887602_609083_60155" xmi:uuid="d219c526-c2ac-44f8-9618-f40e32a41cfa" xmi:type="uml:Property">
        <ownedComment xmi:id="_19_0_4_b1702d9_1702993887627_643365_60311" xmi:uuid="7cbec545-366b-4a92-860e-f044e2071902" xmi:type="uml:Comment">
          <annotatedElement xmi:idref="_19_0_4_b1702d9_1702993887602_609083_60155"/>
          <body>the inherited attribute RelationType. The value of RelationType shall be 'alternate'.</body>
        </ownedComment>
        <name>RelationType</name>
        <visibility>public</visibility>
        <type href="../../../../DataTypes.xmi#STRING"/>
        <defaultValue xmi:id="_19_0_4_b1702d9_1702993887627_139833_60313" xmi:uuid="83915efa-37b6-4acf-9878-815f8add7886" xmi:type="uml:LiteralString">
          <value>alternate</value>
        </defaultValue>
        <redefinedProperty xmi:idref="_18_4_1_e120334_1499417193881_645914_28070"/>
      </ownedAttribute>
      <ownedAttribute xmi:id="_19_0_4_b1702d9_1702993887602_223290_60156" xmi:uuid="59641681-d787-4c4d-b858-ec4685da7663" xmi:type="uml:Property">
